    "username": "emollick",
    "nickname": "Ethan Mollick",
    "text": "Super weird thing about Fable is that it keeps learning about me even with memories and personalization turned off. The thinking traces are full of references to my preferences. Some of it is little notes it writes in various .md files, but maybe it is leaking from elsewhere.",
    "quoted_tweet": null,
    "url": "https://twitter.com/emollick/status/2073956895631593589",
    "time": "2026-07-06 10:27",
    "created_at": "Mon Jul 06 02:27:10 +0000 2026",
    "id_str": "2073956895631593589",
    "is_retweet": false
  },
  {
    "username": "emollick",
    "nickname": "Ethan Mollick",
    "text": "I wonder if Fable might do better at tasks it \"likes\" than those that it doesn't. If you ask it to do something \"Fable-y\" it reacts with enthusiasm and promises to overdeliver. Otherwise, it just gets to work. Testing this would be pretty expensive, so this is all speculation. https://t.co/RuuDClmfpV",
    "quoted_tweet": null,
    "url": "https://twitter.com/emollick/status/2073959909314416756",
